# Naming and Single-Responsibility Audit: Absorption Status and Archive Readiness
File: openOODA/audits/naming/mcode/archive_ready.oot

Provenance: converted from `openOODA/audits/naming-audit-mcode.md` (788 lines). Part 5 of 7.

Redaction note: fleet host names and tailnet addresses are written as generic
placeholders. The audited tree still holds the literals.

## 5. Defect class (d) — Absorption status, and which repos are ready to archive

### 5.1 The structural rule that is not being enforced (F8)

RFC 0012 §2.2 item 5 requires: *"One consolidated binary is installed under its canonical name only. The persona names of
section 2.2 item 4 are accepted as tokens by that binary and are not installed as files."*

Across the fleet, **every absorbed repo still declares `BIN := bin/<name>` and still ships a compiled binary of that name.**
Examples with `bin/` evidence:

- `openOODA-apps/oopdf/bin/oopdf`, `oosheet/bin/oosheet`, `oodeck/bin/oodeck`, `oonotes/bin/oonotes`, `oopaint/bin/oopaint`,
  `oomail/bin/oomail`, `oogit-ui/bin/oogit-ui` — all absorbed personas of `oodocs`/`oocanvas`/`oochat`/`oostudio`, all still
  shipping.
- `openOODA-DE/ooshot/bin/ooshot` (80,944 B), `ooview/bin/ooview` (84,952 B) — absorbed, still shipping.
- `openOODA-kernel/ookernel-mm/bin/ookernel-mm`, `ookernel-iommu/bin/ookernel-iommu`, `ookernel-ipc/bin/ookernel-ipc`,
  `ookernel-ob/bin/ookernel-ob`, `ookernel-unikernel/bin/ookernel-unikernel`, `ookernel-hal-arm64/bin/…`,
  `ookernel-hal-riscv/bin/…`, `oodrv-pci/bin/…`, `oodrv-usb-hid/bin/…`, `oodrv-virtio/bin/…`, `oodrv-display-gop/bin/…` — 12
  kernel repos absorbed, 12 binaries still shipping.
- `openOODA-cloud/oocdn/bin/oocdn`, `oodns-cloud/bin/…`, `oorelay/bin/…`, `ooconsent/bin/…`, `ooregistry-cloud/bin/…`,
  `oostore-cas/bin/…`, `ooqueue/bin/…`, `ooinfer-grid/bin/…`, `oosched-cloud/bin/…` — absorbed, still shipping.
- `openOODA-agents/ooplanner/bin/ooplanner`, `ooarchitect/bin/…`, `ooeval/bin/…`, `ooevolve/bin/…`, `ooredteam/bin/…`,
  `oorelease/bin/…` — absorbed, still shipping.

**Consequence:** the ambiguity in §4 is not a documentation defect — it is a live install-surface defect. The name `ooshot`
denotes a real file and a real subcommand.

